WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.790
Katheryn Winnick has become a breakout star
thanks to her portrayal of legendary shieldmaiden

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.050
Lagertha in the hit series Vikings.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.720
But Vikings is far from the first role Winnick
has nabbed.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.130
In fact, the Canadian actress has been appearing
on film and in TV shows for nearly two decades.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.529
Here's a look at why Lagertha from Vikings
looks so familiar.

00:00:21.529 --> 00:00:23.099
Oh, Canada

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:26.869
Before making the jump to Hollywood, Winnick
earned her stripes appearing in a pair of

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:28.800
TV shows north of the border.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:35.660
In 1999, she landed her screen debut as sorority
girl Suzie in the paranormal drama PSI Factor:

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.370
Chronicles of the Paranormal.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.330
And later that year, she joined the cast of
the high school comedy Student Bodies, where

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.300
she played Holly Benson, girlfriend of main
character Cody Miller.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.190
Hey, everyone has to start somewhere!

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.190
Victimized

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:55.050
Starting in 2002, Winnick began a long and
lucrative side career as a professional victim

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.250
on both the Law and Order and CSI franchises.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:03.391
All told, she's appeared once on Law &amp; Order,
twice on Law &amp; Order: Criminal Intent, and

00:01:03.391 --> 00:01:10.729
managed a CSI trifecta by appearing on CSI:Miami,
CSI:New York, and the original CSI:Crime Scene

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:11.729
Investigation.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:15.909
Over those six appearances, she's managed
to do everything from getting locked in a

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.590
basement by a psycho to being impaled on a
tree.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.170
That's a tough way to make a living.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.439
​Trump Unauthorized

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:30.390
Back in 2005, Winnick played none other than
Donald Trump's first wife Ivana in a TV movie

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.630
called Trump Unauthorized.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:38.090
Variety was less than enthused about Winnick's
work, saying her accent sounded closer to

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:43.319
something from the Rocky and Bullwinkle Show
than it did Czech-born Ivana Trump.

00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:49.530
The Donald himself gave his approval, however,
saying that "Having a two-hour movie on network

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.789
television while you're still living is sort
of wild, you're supposed to be gone for that

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:55.789
to happen."

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:57.429
​Failure to Launch

00:01:57.429 --> 00:02:01.829
Winnick got her first big break with a minor
role in Matthew McConaughey's 2006 romantic

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:07.200
comedy Failure to Launch, a film about a man
in his mid-30s who refuses to leave the comfort

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.190
of his mother's home until he meets the right
woman.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.230
That woman was played by Sarah Jessica Parker,
not Winnick, but Winnick told ShowBizMonkey

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.890
that she would happy to one day take on the
lead role, saying she'd "love to do a romantic

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:22.060
comedy, 100 percent.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.620
You know, they're fun.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.290
Get me a good co-star, someone cute."

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.379
​Killers

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:33.110
Winnick got to live out the fantasy of every
person who bought a ticket to see 2010 hitman-and-wife

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.910
rom-com Killers when she kicked leading man
Ashton Kutcher through a glass door.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:42.590
Most of Winnick's other scenes as Kutcher's
secretary, Vivian, were forgettable, but this

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:47.810
one is notable for being the first time we
got to see the action chops that would later

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.209
make Winnick famous in Vikings.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:52.390
​Love and Other Drugs

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.651
Killers wasn't the only romcom Winnick appeared
in during 2010, as she also had a role in

00:02:57.651 --> 00:03:03.560
Love and Other Drugs, where she got toc make
out with Christina Fandino in front of an

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.519
awestruck Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:09.030
Winnick told reporters that it wasn't just
a cheap stunt.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.930
"This movie is definitely for men and women.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:17.150
Not only do you have that sexiness throughout
the movie, but it's a female character that

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.560
girls can aspire to be…"

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:25.180
Unfortunately, the film didn't take off, and
was another in a string of duds for Winnick.

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:26.200
​Bones

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.799
Winnick met with Bones producers in 2010 about
the "controversial" recurring role of Hannah

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:36.829
Burley, a journalist that FBI agent Seeley
Booth rescues from a terrorist situation in

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:38.049
Afghanistan.

00:03:38.049 --> 00:03:43.140
They warned her that fans might take a disliking
to her for coming between Booth and Brennan.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:48.300
"They definitely want the two of them, Brennan
and Booth, together, so I know I'm gonna be

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.800
in some hot water."

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:55.040
Winnick signed on anyway for a memorable arc
that ended with her turning down Booth's marriage

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:59.290
proposal, allowing him to get back with Brennan
like the fans wanted.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.170
"For a bone, what was your favorite part of
'Bones'?"

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.790
"Booth.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.159
And uh, Bones, obviously."

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:08.270
"Yeah, obviously the bones."

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.060
​Stand Up Guys

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:15.499
In the 2012 crime caper Stand Up Guys, Winnick
played a brothel worker named Oxana.

00:04:15.499 --> 00:04:19.480
Though the film was a flop, the opportunity
to work with some of her favorite actors was

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:24.750
a dream come true for Winnick, who told CraveOnline,
"I really wanted to work with Al Pacino.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:28.980
I'm a huge fan and also love Christopher Walken
and Alan Arkin.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.130
I wanted to share the screen with them and
was excited just to be in the same room as

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.130
them."

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.949
​The Art of the Steal

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:41.919
Chances are you probably missed the 2014 ensemble
comedy The Art of the Steal, which starred

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.409
Kurt Russell as an art thief and featured
Winnick - sporting black hair this time around

00:04:46.409 --> 00:04:48.580
- as his girlfriend Lola.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:53.180
Winnick probably wishes she had missed it
as well, considering it was a critical and

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.699
box office mess.

00:04:54.699 --> 00:04:57.000
Oh well, you can't win 'em all.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.300
​Person of Interest

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:04.280
The cult favorite CBS series Person of Interest
got a visit from a person of particular interest

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.039
to Vikings fans when Winnick guest-starred
in 2015.

00:05:08.039 --> 00:05:12.490
She played Frankie Wells, a bounty hunter
relentlessly stalking her brother's killer.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.970
It's just the kind of high octane, kick-butt
role Winnick is perfect in.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:22.710
Our advice to Winnick: leave the lame romcoms
to Katherine Heigl and stick to punching people

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.919
in the face.

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:25.990
It's what your fans love!

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:26.990
Thanks for watching!

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:29.250
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:32.080
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

